Description: Scalable Library for Eigenvalue Problem Computations (intel + mvapich2, OpenHPC)
 SLEPc is a software library for the solution of large scale sparse
 eigenvalue problems on parallel computers. It is an extension of PETSc
 and can be used for either standard or generalized eigenproblems,
 with real or complex arithmetic.
 Built with the intel compiler family and mvapich2 MPI stack.
 .
 This package is part of the OpenHPC project.
